              {
                "lineHeight": "1.4",
                "fontStyle": "normal",
                "textTransform": "none",
                "textAlign": "left",
                "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
                "fontSize": "28",
                "fontWeight": "400",
                "textDirection": "ltr",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "Ed's setup starts the new loop like Empty tracks, then names tracks 1 to 4 Guitar, Boom, RC20 and Vox and puts one Ed's Rack sound on each track: Acoustic Rhythm 1, Boom Dry, Bass Octave 1 and Vocal Close. The track names come from a published breakdown of Ed Sheeran's pedal; the sounds are our choice, not his settings, and the sheet does not claim otherwise. Inputs, outputs, All tracks, tracks 5 to 8, tempo and pedal setup stay as Empty tracks keeps them. The four new-loop tiles that get a sound are outlined."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "28",
